      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the distance driven:**\n   The odometer reading when picking up his friend is \\(74,568\\) miles, and the odometer reading when dropping him off is \\(74,592\\) miles. The distance driven is:\n   \\[\n   74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the amount of gasoline used:**\n   Ryosuke's car gets \\(28\\) miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gasoline used is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost of the gasoline:**\n   The price of one gallon of gas is \\( \\$4.05 \\). Therefore, the cost of \\( \\frac{6}{7} \\) gallons of gas is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.3}{7} \\approx 3.47 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is \\(\\boxed{3.47}\\).",
