    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Calculate the distance driven**: \n   The odometer reading when Ryosuke picks his friend up is 74,568 miles.\n   The odometer reading when he drops his friend off is 74,592 miles.\n   The distance driven is the difference between these two readings:\n   \\[\n   74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the amount of gas used**: \n   Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. To find out how many gallons of gas were used, we divide the distance driven by the car's fuel efficiency:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cost of the gas used**:\n   The price of one gallon of gas is $4.05. To find the total cost of the gas used, we multiply the amount of gas used by the price per gallon:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\times 4.05 \\text{ dollars per gallon} = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\frac{24.30}{7} = 3.471428571428571 \\approx 3.47 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   Rounding to the nearest cent, the cost is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{3.47}\n   \\]",
